    "detailed_description": "Your chance to defeat Xodar of Gorn! Gunstorm is a single-screen space shooter loaded with playability. Wave after wave of alien craft attack your agile ship. Face various end of level motherships and other special levels.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nUse the mouse to control your ship at the speed of thought, or use the keyboard or game controller. Set your own difficulty level and choose between a fixed or random game for infinite playability. Play the main campaign, or try an Onslaught against foes of increasing speed and number.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nIncludes a variation of the classic arcade game Asteroids.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nYears of work has gone into perfectly balancing the gameplay to make a progressive game that never becomes impossible.",
    "about_the_game": "Your chance to defeat Xodar of Gorn! Gunstorm is a single-screen space shooter loaded with playability. Wave after wave of alien craft attack your agile ship. Face various end of level motherships and other special levels.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nUse the mouse to control your ship at the speed of thought, or use the keyboard or game controller. Set your own difficulty level and choose between a fixed or random game for infinite playability. Play the main campaign, or try an Onslaught against foes of increasing speed and number.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nIncludes a variation of the classic arcade game Asteroids.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nYears of work has gone into perfectly balancing the gameplay to make a progressive game that never becomes impossible.",
    "short_description": "Gunstorm is a space shooter loaded with playability. Wave after wave of alien craft attack your agile ship. Use the mouse to control your ship at the speed of thought in a perfectly balanced game that starts easy and gradually gets more difficult.",
    "supported_languages": "English<strong>*</strong>, French, German<br><strong>*</strong>languages with full audio support",
    "reviews": "\u201cThe gameplay in Gunstorm is pitch perfect. Poorly calculated thrust and overly sensitive ship rotation have ruined more than one Asteroids clone, but that's not the case here; the ship mechanics are spot on...\u201d<br />\r\nGameXtasy<br />\r\n",
